  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A hanging mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> is connected to a four times bigger mass by using a string pulley arrangement, as shown in the figure. The bigger mass is placed on a horizontal ice-slab and being pulled by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>Mg</mi></math> force. In this situation, tension in the string is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>Mg</mi></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo></math>_____. Neglect mass of the string and friction of the block (bigger mass) with ice slab.<br />(Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo></math> acceleration due to gravity)</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0080_b7055609d0f5.png\" style=\"width: 260px; height: 117px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0080_7792a68c5b36.png\" style=\"width: 240px; height: 183px;\" /></p><p>Equation for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>M</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>M</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Equation for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Adding both equation we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>M</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now, tension&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p>"
  }
}